"""Static validation of compiled skills for an agent project.

Authoring checks over the loaded skill catalog, run at train/validate time:

- :func:`validate_skill_loading` — skill directories that fail to parse or
  collide on skill id are reported instead of silently skipped.
- :func:`validate_flow_transitions` — every step's ``next`` resolves to a step
  in the same activation target (or ``END``).
- :func:`validate_links_and_calls` — every ``link``/``call`` target resolves to
  a known skill or ordered block using the runtime's activation lookup, and
  rejects ordered blocks that are internal (``routable: false``).
- :func:`collect_referenced_skill_findings` — every compiled ``referenced_skills``
  entry resolves in the catalog.
- :func:`collect_hidden_prose_skill_reference_findings` — prose ``@skill``
  tokens must not target ``hidden: true`` skills (YAML ``call`` / ``link``
  and ``resolve_with`` remain allowed).
- :func:`collect_referenced_block_findings` — every compiled ``referenced_blocks``
  entry resolves to an ordered block on the same skill.
- :func:`collect_import_tools_findings` — every ``import_tools`` entry resolves
  to a shared project-root tool.
- :func:`validate_responses_and_actions` — ordered-block actions/utterances reference
  responses that exist or built-in actions the step executor can dispatch.
- :func:`validate_tool_and_verbatim_refs` — tool ``on_success`` / ``on_failure``,
  skill ``utter:`` triggers, and ``requires_confirmation`` ask/denial names:
  response names exist and referenced bodies are non-whitespace.
- :func:`validate_cancel_skill_confirmation_refs` — the same ask/denial check
  for ``orchestrator.tool_constraints.cancel``.
- :func:`~rasa.mantle.content.validation.validate_response_variants`
  — per-variant CRV checks (non-empty text, condition syntax, readable memory
  refs, default-variant rules) with ``responses.yml`` location in findings.
- :func:`validate_default_skills` — every bundled default skill actually
  loaded.
- :func:`validate_skill_identifiers` — skill ids avoid reserved memory
  namespaces, dots, and the default-skill routing flag.
- :func:`validate_skill_descriptions` — every skill has a non-empty
  ``description`` (the orchestrator routes on that text).
- :func:`validate_ordered_block_structure` — a blocks-only skill has
  exactly one entry block, and every other block is reachable from it.
- :func:`collect_incomplete_prose_at_token_findings` — error when instruction
  bodies contain incomplete ``@skill`` / ``@block`` / ``@tool`` lookalikes
  (must be one id after the prefix).
- :func:`collect_bundled_default_skill_authoring_findings` — the same
  description and incomplete-token checks on bundled default skills.
- :func:`validate_prose_instruction_scopes` — prose ``if:`` conditions are
  non-empty, use supported expression constructs, and reference memory
  readable while that skill is active (own public and private fields,
  other skills' public fields, and project memory).
- :func:`validate_prose_memory_references` — ``@memory`` tokens in outer
  prose bodies and ordered-block ``AutonomousStep.instructions`` name memory
  readable while that skill is active (same rules as
  :func:`~rasa.mantle.memory.manager.readable_memory_slot_names`).
- :func:`collect_incomplete_memory_reference_findings` — error when instruction
  bodies contain incomplete ``@memory`` lookalikes that cannot be substituted
  (must be ``@memory.<namespace>.<entry>``).
- :func:`collect_session_reference_in_instruction_findings` — error when
  instruction **bodies** contain ``session.<namespace>.<entry>`` (``if:``
  conditions keep ``session.*``; prose should use ``@memory.…``).
- :func:`validate_execute_step_parameters` — ``execute_tool`` parameter values
  that look like ``session.*`` references are canonical two-level forms and
  name memory readable while that skill is active; plain literals pass.

Checks return :class:`~rasa.mantle.validation_finding.ValidationFinding`
objects rather than raising, so :func:`rasa.mantle.validation.validate_project`
can aggregate them with the other project checks and report every problem at
once.
"""

